\description{
\code{ucip.bayes()} estimates a single participant's deviation from the
unlimited-capacity independent-parallel (UCIP) benchmark.
\code{capacityGroup.bayes()} partially pools participant effects in a
hierarchical model. Both functions use the Houpt-Townsend score statistic
also used by \code{\link[=ucip.test]{ucip.test()}}.
}
\details{
Three effect scales are available. \code{score} uses
\eqn{\theta_i = U_i/V_i}, the Peto one-step log hazard-ratio estimate, with
precision \eqn{V_i}. It is the default and satisfies
\eqn{Cz_i = \theta_i\sqrt{V_i}}. \code{standardized} reports the same model on
the reference-\eqn{Cz} scale,
\eqn{\phi_i = \theta_i\sqrt{V_{\mathrm{ref}}}}. The default priors are
transformed by the same factor, so \code{score} and \code{standardized} differ only
in units. \code{multiplicative} estimates
\eqn{\eta_i = \log(A_i/B_i)}, the log weighted-capacity ratio, using a
delta-method precision. \code{capacity} is retained as an alias for
\code{multiplicative}.

Default priors are anchored on the \code{score} scale:
\eqn{\mu_\theta \sim N(0, 0.5^2)},
\eqn{\tau_\theta \sim \mathrm{HalfNormal}(0, 0.5)}, or
\eqn{\tau_\theta^2 \sim \mathrm{InvGamma}(2, 0.25)} for the conjugate
sampler. On the \code{standardized} scale, standard deviations are multiplied by
\eqn{\sqrt{V_{\mathrm{ref}}}} and the inverse-gamma rate by
\eqn{V_{\mathrm{ref}}}. The \code{multiplicative} defaults are 0.35 for both
standard deviations and \eqn{0.35^2} for the inverse-gamma rate.

\code{ucip.bayes()} uses an analytic normal-normal posterior. A one-participant,
one-condition call to \code{capacityGroup.bayes()} is routed to that analysis.
Group fits use either a conjugate Gibbs sampler (\code{InvGamma}) or a Stan NUTS
model with a half-normal prior on the between-participant standard deviation
(\code{HalfNormal} or \code{Centered}).
}
